  <data name="BugCheck_Unknown_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Unknown Windows kernel crash code.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_Unknown_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Recommend searching for this crash code online for tailored resolution.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000000A_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kernel attempted to access pageable memory at an elevated IRQL.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000000A_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usually caused by buggy or incompatible device drivers, or faulty memory. Recommend updating suspect drivers or running Windows Memory Diagnostic.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000001E_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A kernel-mode program generated an exception which the error handler did not catch.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000001E_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Often related to newly installed hardware, faulty drivers, or conflicting system services. Try rolling back recent updates.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000003B_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>An exception happened while executing a system service routine.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000003B_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Frequently caused by graphics drivers or corrupted system files. Recommend clean reinstalling GPU drivers and running sfc /scannow.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000050_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Invalid system memory was referenced.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000050_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Commonly caused by faulty RAM, damaged slots, antivirus kernel drivers, or disk file corruption. Clean RAM contacts or run memory checks.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000007E_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A system thread generated an exception that the error handler did not catch.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000007E_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usually caused by incompatible drivers or insufficient disk space. Check the suspect module name and update its driver.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000009F_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A driver is in an inconsistent or invalid power state, often during sleep/wake.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000009F_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Often caused by power management, USB controllers, or Wi-Fi drivers failing to transition states during sleep/wake. Update chipset drivers.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x000000A0_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The power manager experienced a fatal internal error.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x000000A0_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usually related to a corrupted hiberfil.sys file or storage driver issues. Try running powercfg -h off followed by powercfg -h on to rebuild.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x000000D1_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A driver attempted to access an invalid memory address at an elevated IRQL.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x000000D1_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>One of the most common crash codes. Identify the faulting driver and install the latest official release.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x000000EF_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A critical system process terminated unexpectedly.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x000000EF_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Indicates a vital OS process died, often due to system corruption, malware, or failing disk. Run DISM and SFC repair.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000101_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>An expected clock interrupt on a secondary processor was not received within the allocated interval.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000101_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Classic CPU stability issue: unstable overclock, insufficient Vcore voltage, thermal throttling, or outdated BIOS. Reset BIOS to defaults.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000116_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The display driver failed to respond, and the attempt to reset and recover timed out.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000116_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>GPU hang: GPU driver crashed, overheating, inadequate power, or failing GPU hardware. Reinstall GPU drivers with DDU and monitor temperatures.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000124_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A fatal hardware error occurred, detected by Windows Hardware Error Architecture.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000124_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fatal physical hardware fault: CPU failure/undervoltage, disconnecting NVMe SSD, bad RAM, or PCIe bus errors. Check hardware and power supply.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000133_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The DPC watchdog detected a prolonged DPC run time or accumulated time.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000133_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Frequently caused by outdated SSD firmware, storage controller driver delays, or faulty Wi-Fi drivers. Update SSD firmware and chipset drivers.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000139_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The kernel detected corruption of a critical data structure.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000139_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Driver buffer overflow, damaged system libraries, or memory bit flips. Check drivers and memory stability.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000154_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The memory manager store component caught an unexpected exception.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x00000154_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Often caused by a failing SSD/HDD, drive dropping off the bus, or storage controller driver crash. Immediately back up important data.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000001A_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A severe memory management error occurred.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="BugCheck_0x0000001A_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Commonly caused by failing RAM sticks, unstable XMP/EXPO profiles, or corrupted pagefiles. Disable RAM overclocking and test memory.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AppException_Unknown_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Application encountered an unhandled exception code.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AppException_Unknown_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ensure the application is updated to its latest version.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AppException_0xC0000005_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Memory access violation (the thread attempted to read from or write to a virtual address without proper access).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AppException_0xC0000005_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Usually caused by software null pointer dereference, incompatible plugins, or corrupted program files. Try updating or reinstalling the app.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AppException_0xC0000409_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Stack buffer overrun (triggered fast-fail security protection).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AppException_0xC0000409_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Internal program bug causing stack corruption, terminating via fast-fail mechanism. Check for application updates.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AppException_0xC0000374_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A heap corruption has been detected.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AppException_0xC0000374_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
